{"scene_description":"The image depicts a warehouse interior with stacks of red plastic crates and pallets. The perspective is from the ground level, looking upwards towards the ceiling. There are two large stacks of red crates on either side of the frame, with one stack in the foreground and another in the background. In between these stacks, there is a forklift moving through the space, carrying a load of crates. The floor appears to be made of concrete, and the ceiling has fluorescent lighting. On the right side of the image, there are stacks of white boxes or packages. The overall scene suggests an active storage area or distribution center."}

{"objects":[{"id":1,"label":"red plastic crate stack (foreground)","observation":"A tall stack of red plastic crates is positioned in the foreground, with multiple levels of crates stacked on top of each other. The crates appear to be uniform in size and shape, and they are arranged neatly on wooden pallets. The crates have white labels on them, but the text is not legible from this angle."},{"id":2,"label":"red plastic crate stack (background)","observation":"In the background, there is another tall stack of red plastic crates. This stack is similar in appearance to the foreground stack, with multiple levels of crates stacked on top of each other. The crates are also arranged on wooden pallets, and the white labels on the crates are visible but not legible from this angle."},{"id":3,"label":"forklift","observation":"A forklift is moving through the space, carrying a load of red plastic crates. The forklift is black and orange, and it is positioned between the two stacks of crates. The forklift's wheels are in contact with the concrete floor, and its forks are holding the crates securely."},{"id":4,"label":"white box/package stacks (right side)","observation":"On the right side of the image, there are stacks of white boxes or packages. These stacks are taller than the red crate stacks, and they appear to be organized in rows. The white boxes are uniform in size and shape, and they are arranged neatly on wooden pallets."}]}

